{"path":"ranges/zip_view/sentinel/operator-","title":"operator-(ranges::zip_view::sentinel)","titleHtml":"operator-<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(ranges::zip_view::<i>sentinel</i>)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/zip_view/sentinel/operator-","section":"ranges","kind":"page","summary":"Computes the minimal distance between the underlying tuple of iterators of x and the underlying tuple of sentinels of y.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> OtherConst <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; requires <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/sized_sentinel_for\"><span class=\"kw2881\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sized_sentinel_for</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2909\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">sentinel_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*maybe-const*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Const, Views<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2908\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iterator_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*maybe-const*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>OtherConst, Views<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> ...<span class=\"br0\">)</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">friend</span> <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/common_type\"><span class=\"kw641\">std::<span class=\"me2\">common_type_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range_size_t\"><span class=\"kw2910\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">range_difference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*maybe-const*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>OtherConst, Views<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span>...<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>operator<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> iterator<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>OtherConst<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> x, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> sentinel<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> y <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> OtherConst <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; requires <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/sized_sentinel_for\"><span class=\"kw2881\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sized_sentinel_for</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2909\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">sentinel_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*maybe-const*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Const, Views<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2908\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iterator_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*maybe-const*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>OtherConst, Views<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> ...<span class=\"br0\">)</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">friend</span> <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/common_type\"><span class=\"kw641\">std::<span class=\"me2\">common_type_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range_size_t\"><span class=\"kw2910\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">range_difference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*maybe-const*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>OtherConst, Views<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span>...<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>operator<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> sentinel<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> y, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> iterator<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>OtherConst<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> x <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Computes the minimal distance between the underlying tuple of iterators of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code> and the underlying tuple of sentinels of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">y</span></code>.\n</p><p>These functions are not visible to ordinary <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/unqualified_lookup\">unqualified</a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/qualified_lookup\">qualified lookup</a>, and can only be found by <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/adl\">argument-dependent lookup</a> when <code>zip_view::<i>sentinel</i>&lt;Const&gt;</code> is an associated class of the arguments.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> x\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> an <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/zip_view/iterator\">iterator</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> y\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> a <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/zip_view/sentinel\">sentinel</a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Let <code><i>current_</i></code> denote the underlying tuple of iterators of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code>, and <code><i>end_</i></code> denote the underlying tuple of sentinels of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">y</span></code>.\n</p><p>Let <code><i>DIST</i>(x, y, i)</code> be a distance calculated by expression equivalent to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">get</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>i<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>x.<span class=\"me1\">current_</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">get</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>i<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>y.<span class=\"me1\">end_</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> for some integer <code>i</code>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> the value with the smallest absolute value among <code><i>DIST</i>(x, y, i)</code> of all <code>i</code> in range <code>0 ≤ i &lt; sizeof...(Views)</code></div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>x <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> y<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cassert&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;deque&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;list&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;ranges&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;vector&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> x <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector\"><span class=\"kw1277\">std::<span class=\"me2\">vector</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">4</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> y <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/deque\"><span class=\"kw1279\">std::<span class=\"me2\">deque</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">'a'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'b'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'c'</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> z <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu16\">1.1</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">2.2</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> w <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/list\"><span class=\"kw1283\">std::<span class=\"me2\">list</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> p <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/zip_view\"><span class=\"kw3715\">views::<span class=\"me2\">zip</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>x, y, z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw778\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> p.<span class=\"me1\">end</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw778\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p.<span class=\"me1\">end</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> p.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>maybe_unused<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> q <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/zip_view\"><span class=\"kw3715\">views::<span class=\"me2\">zip</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>x, y, w<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// The following code fires a compile-time error because std::list::iterator</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// does not support operator- that is needed to calculate the distance:</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// auto e = q.begin() - q.end();</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"},{"path":"ranges/zip_view","title":"std::ranges::views::zip, std::ranges::zip_view"},{"path":"ranges/zip_view/sentinel","title":"std::ranges::zip_view<Views...>::sentinel"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"operator-(ranges::zip_view::sentinel)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++23. Computes the minimal distance between the underlying tuple of iterators of x and the underlying tuple of sentinels of y."},{"label":"Parameters","